ite notes from originals already received. I have not seen the exact quote in this context. Risk: quoting without exact text. I need the exact quote for evidence. Better to recall pages 45-46 again? That would consume requests. Actually recalling doesn't count as model call? Each action is a model call presumably (20 requests left).\n\nHmm. I have limited visibility. The safest: write multi_agent note now updating generative_agents_evaluators=100 with the exact quote from page 47 which I can see: \"Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators.\" Good.\n\nFor CAMEL, I need the quote from page 45 or 46. I'll recall page 45-46 to get text (delivered next batch alongside pending). Actually pending batch already queued 49-52. I can recall 45/46 again but that may delay.\n\nLet me just update the multi_agent note with the 100 evaluators quote and keep the CAMEL pending marker, then read the remaining batch. Actually better: do the note write now with confirmed facts.\n\nActually the delivery system: my action writes a note; then next action the next batch is delivered. Let me write the note.\n\nNote content under 1500 chars. Include page numbers and quotes.\n\nBut CAMEL prompting answer needs to be in the final note eventually. I'll add later after re-reading pages 45-46.\n\nLet me write the note now."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8871, "completion_tokens": 836, "total_tokens": 9707, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4224}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 443}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4224, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 4647}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
