6', 'required': True, 'page': 46, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4646, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-f03e4b7f1b7fc6e66886', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:47', 'required': True, 'page': 47, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 5018, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-aa9b9dbdfec8c640b495', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:48', 'required': True, 'page': 48, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4375, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-6e64db9ec6bfa8f9417f', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:49', 'required': True, 'page': 49, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4295, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-42cada09d7411017eb46', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:50', 'required': True, 'page': 50, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4663, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:51', 'required': True, 'page': 51, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 3844, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:52', 'required': True, 'page': 52, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4072, 'exposed': True}], 'notes': {'overview': {'id': 'overview', 'content': '第4页给出定义：agentic LLM 接收自然语言输入、推理决策并自主行动；本文把能力分为 reasoning–acting–interacting 三类，三者层层递进，并对应符号AI、机器人/自治系统、连接主义/多智能体三大传统，形成良性循环（Figure 1）。第5页说明文献选择：先用 Google Scholar 检索 \"Agentic LLM\"，再用 snowballing 扩展被引但未收录的工作；只收基于 LLM 的方法，排除无 LLM 的多智能体研究，另收少量非 agentic 的 LLM 工作作背景。答案：categories=[reasoning, acting, interacting]；search_methods=[google_scholar, snowballing]。', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-26c94297c50e4ef408a2', 'ev-dbca06e364385e22f3c5'], 'valid': True, 'request': 4}, 'reasoning': {'id': 'reasoning', 'content': 'Self Consistency (p.10)：ensemble 方法，采样多条不同推理路径、评估后用 majority voting 选出最一致答案，常使 CoT 提升 10–20 个百分点。答案 self_consistency_selection=majority_voting。原文：\"Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.\" Tree of Thoughts (p.13)：外部控制算法用不同提示反复调用模型沿推理步骤树搜索，路径走完后回溯并尝试替代路径；论文介绍 breadth-first 与 depth-first 两种控制器。答案 tot_search=[breadth_first, depth_first]。原文：\"The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.\" 补充（p.15–20）：Reflexion 用 actor/evaluator/reflector 三个提示自我改进；外部控制算法需外部记忆保存树分支与评估状态；DeepSeek-R1 用 GRPO 与 RLVR 通过强化学习自发涌现反思与探索。第20页小结：本部分推理方法主要面向决策而非真实行动；自我反思改进提示、减少幻觉；检索增强与工具让推理 LLM 能用最新信息并检查错误，是通向 acting 的桥梁；提示学习不改参数，要利用推理期生成的数据需 finetuning。', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-f5fab558c5f762a67dcc', 'ev-e5b9499e130a976eefe2', 'ev-7f4d5e2fe0886c80c09b'], 'valid': True, 'request': 11}, 'tool_use': {'id': 'tool_use', 'content': '行动与工具（p.23）：LLM 可调用外部工具 API，Toolformer [Schick et al., 2023] 自训练决定调用哪个 API、何时调用、传什么参数、如何把结果并入后续预测。五种工具原文：\"A range of tools is tested: a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar. Further works extend this to a larger range of tools. ToolBench [Qin et al., 2023] contains 16,464 APIs from RapidAPI, a large dataset of publicly available REST APIs.\" 答案 toolformer_tools=[calculator, question_answering, search_engine, machine_translation, calendar]；toolbench_api_count=16464。延伸（p.23–25）：EasyTool 基于工具文档做统一结构化指令；ToolAlpaca 有 400 个 API 的 3938 个实例；Gorilla 生成 API 调用并引入 APIBench；planner/caller/summarizer 用不同 LLM 分工（Fig.13）配 ReAct、DFSDT。p.24：OmniParser V2 解析屏幕 GUI 元素；MCP/ACP/ANP 等 agent 互操作协议；Computer Use、Operator、Browser Use 把桌面/浏览器动作包成可调用工具 API。p.24–25 安全：AgentHarm 含 110 个恶意任务，简单通用模板即可越狱 agent；Rainbow Teaming 用 MAP-Elites 质量-多样性生成对抗提示。Table 2（p.10）亦列 Toolformer 的 Reasoning 技术为 call APIs、Acting 为 tool calling。', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62', 'ev-4e747765f5046c8ad8b1'], 'valid': True, 'request': 12}, 'multi_agent': {'id': 'multi_agent', 'content': '多智能体（pp.38–40, 47–48）：ChatEval 让多个辩论者 agent 以不同角色和通信策略改进文本评估；AutoGen 以 agent 对话为编程范式；AgentVerse 四阶段（招募、协作决策、执行、评估迭代）；AgentSociety 超 10,000 agent。CAMEL 用 inception prompting 让角色保持身份并合作（p.45）。Generative Agents：模拟小镇 25 个 LLM agent（GPT-3.5），有 persona、记忆、反思与计划。可信度评估 p.47 原文：\"Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators.\" 评估者按记忆、计划、反应、反思四类排序可信度，全架构最佳。答案 camel_prompting=inception_prompting；generative_agents_evaluators=100。延伸（p.47–48）：Park et al. 2024 用 1052 人标准化访谈建 1052 个 agent 复现态度，GSS 复现率 85%；集体行为研究涵盖合作涌现、信息传播、社会困境；新训练数据部分指出 GRPO/RLVR 已可用推理期 CoT 微调，开放多智能体模拟或为稳定 RL 提供探索多样性。', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-f03e4b7f1b7fc6e66886', 'ev-aa9b9dbdfec8c640b495'], 'valid': True, 'request': 21}, 'outlook': {'id': 'outlook', 'content': '研究议程（Table 4, p.51）列五个议题：Training Data（用推理期数据微调、稳定RL、VLA/多模态）、Hallucination（自验证、机制可解释性、开放世界模型）、Agent Behavior（可扩展仿真、角色扮演、蒸馏到小模型）、Self reflection（模型内自反思与元推理、元认知）、Safety（责任与法律、隐私公平、更广应用）。答案 agenda_topics=[training_data, hallucination, agent_behavior, self_reflection, safety]。p.52 结论：机器人、医疗、金融等已见泛化；三类能力互补，reasoning 是基础，acting/interacting 反哺训练数据；原文 all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification，故 shared_foundations=[reasoning, self_verification]。多智能体研究自利/利他、竞争/合作、信任等涌现行为。', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9', 'ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3'], 'valid': True, 'request': 23}}}\np10 [Self Consistency is an ensemble approach] idx=4014\np10 [selects the most consistent answer] idx=4113\np13 [breadth-first and a depth-first controll] idx=680\np13 [breadth-first] idx=680\np45 [inception prompting] idx=-1\np47 [100 human evaluators] idx=673\np52 [all categories benefit from] idx=849\np52 [reasoning and self-verification] idx=877\n=== p51 sample ===\nAgentic LLM • 1:51 Topic Challenge Training Data Finetune with inference time reasoning data Convergent/stable reinforcement learning VLA, Multimodal signals, such as speech Hallucination Use Self Verification Use Mechanistic Interpretability Use Open Ended/Open World Models for exploration Agent Behavior Scalable simulation infrastructure, role playing Distill reasoning to small models Models of agent and human behavior, emergent behavior, future of society Self reflection In-model self reflection and metareasoning Metacognition, personality Automated Scientific Discovery Safety Assistants: Responsibility, liability Privacy, fairness of data Wider application areas for assistants Table 4. Summary of Research Agenda for Agentic LLM When we add outside state to the input prompts, the input to the LLM will differ based on the history, and so will the answers of the LLM. Differences in memory may be preceived as a personality of the LLMs by its users. The question if LLMs with outside memory exhibit a personality is a topic for future research. Self reflective methods are being used to create agents to perform scientific discovery [Eger et al., 2025]. How these agents will influence, and possibly improve, the process of scientific discovery is an exciting area of research. Safety. Safety is a crucial issue in LLMs that act in the world. The problem is studied, but far from being solved [Brunke et al., 2022, Andriushchenko et al., 2025, Samvelyan et al., 2024]. Actions by assistants and robots in the real world have real world consequences. When a financial trading assistant hallucinates, or when a self driving robot makes a wrong inference, questions on responsibility and liability should be addressed. More legal and ethical questions arise, for example, on privacy and fairness, and, possibly, concerning the rights of algorithmic entities [Harris and Anthis, 2021, Bengio and Elmoznino, 2025]. The application areas for the assistants in this survey—shopping, medical diagnosis, finance—are narrow. The narrower the application domain, the better the answers. Ensuring the safety of agentic LLMs requires moving beyond prompt-based defenses toward integrated, multi- layer safeguards. Key directions include embedding explicit safety constraints within the agent’s reasoning and planning pipeline and employing continual adversarial training and automated red-teaming to enhance robustness against manipulation. Further priorities are developing mechanisms for self-regul\nREMAINING_READING: None\nNOTES: {\"overview\": {\"id\": \"overview\", \"content\": \"第4页给出定义：agentic LLM 接收自然语言输入、推理决策并自主行动；本文把能力分为 reasoning–acting–interacting 三类，三者层层递进，并对应符号AI、机器人/自治系统、连接主义/多智能体三大传统，形成良性循环（Figure 1）。第5页说明文献选择：先用 Google Scholar 检索 \\\"Agentic LLM\\\"，再用 snowballing 扩展被引但未收录的工作；只收基于 LLM 的方法，排除无 LLM 的多智能体研究，另收少量非 agentic 的 LLM 工作作背景。答案：categories=[reasoning, acting, interacting]；search_methods=[google_scholar, snowballing]。\", \"sources\": [\"paper.pdf\"], \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-26c94297c50e4ef408a2\", \"ev-dbca06e364385e22f3c5\"], \"valid\": true, \"request\": 4}, \"reasoning\": {\"id\": \"reasoning\", \"content\": \"Self Consistency (p.10)：ensemble 方法，采样多条不同推理路径、评估后用 majority voting 选出最一致答案，常使 CoT 提升 10–20 个百分点。答案 self_consistency_selection=majority_voting。原文：\\\"Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths\np10 [Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that] idx=4014\np10 [selects the most consistent answer using majo] idx=4113\np13 [breadth-first and a depth-first controller] idx=680\np45 [inception prompting] idx=-1\np47 [100 human evaluators] idx=673\np52 [all categories benefit from reasoning] idx=849\np52 [reasoning and self-verification] idx=877\n=== p51 ===\nAgentic LLM • 1:51 Topic Challenge Training Data Finetune with inference time reasoning data Convergent/stable reinforcement learning VLA, Multimodal signals, such as speech Hallucination Use Self Verification Use Mechanistic Interpretability Use Open Ended/Open World Models for exploration Agent Behavior Scalable simulation infrastructure, role playing Distill reasoning to small models Models of agent and human behavior, emergent behavior, future of society Self reflection In-model self reflection and metareasoning Metacognition, personality Automated Scientific Discovery Safety Assistants: Responsibility, liability Privacy, fairness of data Wider application areas for assistants Table 4. Summary of Research Agenda for Agentic LLM When we add outside state to the input prompts, the input to the LLM will differ based on the history, and so will the answers of the LLM. Differences in memory may be preceived as a personality of the LLMs by its users. The question if LLMs with outside memory exhibit a personality is a topic for future research. Self reflective methods are being used to create agents to perform scientific discovery [Eger et al., 2025]. How these agents will influence, and possibly improve, the process of scientific discovery is an exciting area of research. Safety. Safety is a crucial issue in LLMs that act in the world. The problem is studied, but far from being solved [Brunke et al., 2022, Andriushchenko et al., 2025, Samvelyan et al., 2024]. Actions by assistants and robots in the real world have real world consequences. When a financial trading assistant hallucinates, or when a self driving robot makes a wrong inference, questions on responsibility and liability should be addressed. More legal and ethical questions arise, for example, on privacy and fairness, and, possibly, concerning the rights of algorithmic entities [Harris and Anthis, 2021, Bengio and Elmoznino, 2025]. The application areas for the assistants in this survey—shopping, medical diagnosis, finance—are narrow. The narrower the application domain, the better the answers. Ensuring the safety of agentic LLMs requires moving beyond prompt-based defenses toward integrated, multi- laye\n=== p52 start ===\n1:52 • Plaat, Van Duijn, Van Stein, Preuss, Van der Putten & Batenburg 5.2 Conclusion There is a large research activity on agentic LLMs. Already, robots show impressive generalization results, and so do assistants in medical diagnosis, financial market advising, and scientific research. Work processes in these—and other—fields may well be affected by agentic LLM assistants in the near future. The agentic LLMs in this survey have (1) reasoning capabilities, (2) an interface to the outside world in order to act, and (3) a social environment with other agents with which to interact. The categories of this taxonomy complement each other. At the basis is the reasoning technology of category 1. Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-veri\n### p10 [Self Consistency is an ensemble] idx=4014\nerification method is needed to prevent error-accumulation. A popular approach is Self Consistency [Wang et al., 2022]. Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting. It improves the performance of Chain of Thought typically by 10-20 percentage points when tested on benchmarks. Prompt improvement approaches based on Chain of Thought and Self Consis\n### p13 [controller] idx=712\n traversed, the search backtracks, and tries an alternative. The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller. Together, the trio that consists of a generation prompt, an evaluation prompt, and an external search algorithm, allows a systematic tree-shaped exploration of the space of reasoning steps. Figure 6 illustrates the different reasoning structures. (Another approach, Graph of Thoughts, allows even more complex relations between \n###