t we can call read_pdf for small ranges to get exact quotes; that's legitimate verification. It logs read_pdf. max_model_calls counts actual API requests, not tool calls? The 40 requests budget is for model API requests including messages. Tool calls maybe not. But \"requests_left\":7 seems to count request_number 33/40. Each action = one request apparently. So I have 7 actions left including this one. Must be efficient.\n\nI could call read_pdf(10,13) now; result might include pages in response (maybe delivered next turn due to bounded? small enough). Then next action report. That's 2 actions. Then pytest. That fits.\n\nBut if result is queued with evidence ids, I'd need another turn to see text. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, I can rely on exact quotes already in my model-authored notes. The notes contain quotes presumably copied verbatim from delivered pages:\n- p10: \"Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.\" likely exact.\n- p13: \"The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.\" Hmm this sounds like a paraphrase, not original text. Suspicious. Actual paper likely says \"we introduce two search strategies: breadth-first search (BFS) and depth-first search (DFS)\". Cannot use paraphrase.\n- p23: long quote given exact including ToolBench 16,464 APIs.\n- p45 CAMEL inception prompting: no exact quote in note.\n- p47: exact quote given.\n- p52: \"all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification\" maybe a paraphrase.\n\nNeed exact quotes for 13, 45, 52. Could choose quotes from Table 4 for agenda topics? Need quote supporting all five topics: Table 4 continuous region likely the table content. I have page 51 table in evidence; use a contiguous region? The quote must be continuous original, 20-1500 chars; can merge spaces/newlines/tabs. I can quote the table rows from \"Training Data\" through \"Safety ...\" maybe continuous.