\nActually better: do recall AND then in next action write report? Risky if pending batch doesn't include pages I need. Let's do recall first and see.\n\nAlternatively use read_pdf for pages 10-13 and 45-52 in one command that prints only keyword lines — but that duplicates reads. The feedback said don't reread unchanged sources. But I do need quotes.\n\nLet me do recall of pending ids first — those are likely pages covering the second half (45-52) maybe.\n\nI'll write a compact action: recall pending ids.\n\nPlan says merge notes into report.json doing. I could also start writing report.json with what I'm confident in, then adjust. But writes cost requests too.\n\nAction: recall pending evidence."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8721, "completion_tokens": 1554, "total_tokens": 10275, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4352}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1447}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4352, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 4369}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
